*> Implementation test of the climate sampler and the multi-noise biome lookup (core/src/climate.cob; T0413; docs/protocol/10
*> sections 7.1 to 7.3, 13.2, 13.4): the six router functions of the fixture tree (the noises and shifts of 6.1 with the
*> real noise definitions; the offset spline of the depth is a small fixture one) evaluate and quantise as
*> (long)(v * 10000.0f); at the quart cells of the worked examples of 13.2 (seed 0) the temperature, humidity,
*> continentalness, erosion and weirdness equal the document's values (1182 -13 -81 -1039 111 at (0, 16, 0), ...);
*> the depth is the fixture's, from the independent reference. The lookup returns the point of the smallest fitness
*> (sum of squared distances plus the squared offset), the earlier point on a tie, over a table of five points
*> (two with the same ranges tie; one carries an offset), and over the five points of the Nether preset
*> (BIOME-SOURCE-POINT of the content library).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CLIMATE.
